    "q-105226": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105226",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If $A=\\{1,3,5,7,9\\}$ and $B=\\{2,4,6,8,10\\},$ then $B∖A=$",
      "worked_solution": "The set $B∖A$ is the set of all elements belonging to $B$ but *not* $A.$ Note that no elements of $A$ are also in $B.$  Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B∖A & =B-A \\\\  & =\\{2,4,6,8,10\\}-\\{1,3,5,7,9\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,4,6,8,10\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
